    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.diff\n\n### Description\n\nYou currently have to choose between two view styles (sign or number). I’d like to suggest the ability to disable this feature entirely for a potential performance boost by introducing an option like `view.style = false`.\n\nThe rationale is that I don’t find the signs necessary since I can simply use `git status` for an overview. What I truly value is the `toggle_overlay` feature, which provides an efficient way to view diffs in the current file. I haven’t found a better alternative for this functionality.\n\nDisabling the signs aligns well with the plugin's primary purpose—diffing. The signs are more of an optional QoL feature rather than a core necessity.",
