    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\n> Disabling the signs aligns well with the plugin's primary purpose—diffing. The signs are more of an optional QoL feature rather than a core necessity.\n\nI very much do not agree with this as interactive visualization of diff regions via signs or number colors [*is*](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/4446e834c30c799627d65691c73d59638e5c965f/doc/mini-diff.txt#L10-L13) the primary purpose of 'mini.diff'. Everything else is a nice quality of life improvement.\n\nThat said, allowing to disable that visualization should be relatively straightforward. I'll look into it.",
