        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "After almost having `view.style = 'none'` implemented, I noticed that it itself comes at a performance cost for a primary use cases of actually visualizing hunks (as there are at least two extra `if style ~= 'none' then` checks which for most users are not needed).\n\nAfter actually measuring the speed improvement of `view.style = 'none'`, I am leaning towards not having this implemented.  Hunk data still needs to be computed and cycled through to account for overlay visualization. Visualizing hunks in signcolumn or by colored line numbers is *very* fast as it uses Neovim's extmark feature (which essentially powers LSP semantic and tree-sitter highlighting).\n\nAn overhead of actually placing extmarks from about a minute of very intensive editing simulation to stress test this case was about 4 milliseconds. I find this acceptable when an alternative is to add a bit more code complexity via nesting behind `if style ~= 'none' then` conditions and actually decreasing performance for much more common use cases (albeit *very* minor).\n\nSo I am afraid I am going to close this as not planned. Thanks for the suggestion, though!",
