        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> I would also appreciate this feature. [CodeCompanion](https://codecompanion.olimorris.dev/configuration/chat-buffer.html#diff) currently only supports mini.diff for diff overlays, but I would like to keep using gitsigns for visualizing hunks.\n\nSo if I understand correctly, you'd like to still use 'mini.diff' for toggle-able overlay, but have it not show signs? I think for all intents and purposes, the following setup should achieve that:\n\n```lua\nrequire('mini.diff').setup({\n  view = { style = 'number', priority = 1 },\n})\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniDiffSignAdd', {})\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniDiffSignChange', {})\nvim.api.nvim_set_hl(0, 'MiniDiffSignDelete', {})\n```",
